{
  "tutorial": {
    "id": 4545,
    "version": 2,
    "type": "course",
    "isNew": false,
    "codeLanguage": "javascript",
    "title": "Extending Classes",
    "descriptionContent": "Learn how to write new classes based on other classes' functionality.",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17687,
        "title": "Inheritance",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 150007,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Imagine we're making an adventure game. The characters in the game have a lot in common, but they're also different in many ways.</p><p>That's where <strong>inheritance</strong> comes into play.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 150008,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can create a <code>Character</code> class to bundle the <strong>main features</strong> of the characters.</p><p>Then, using inheritance, we can <em>extend</em> it with <strong>additional functionality</strong> for different character types.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 150009,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To inherit features from a class, we need to use the <code>extends</code> keyword in the class definition.</p><p>By coding <code>extends</code>, we'll make the <code>Player</code> class inherit from the <code>Character</code> class.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"84\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Character\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Character\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>extends</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 150010,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Inheritance gives a class all the <strong>properties and methods</strong> of the class it's extending or inheriting from.</p><p>See it for yourself: create an object from the <code>Player</code> class and display it.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"113\" endIndex=\"116\" /><option startIndex=\"117\" endIndex=\"123\" /><option startIndex=\"124\" endIndex=\"132\" /><option startIndex=\"147\" endIndex=\"153\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Character\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Character\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Player(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Ranger&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(player);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>new</code> followed by <code>Player</code> and then <code>\"Ranger\"</code>, <code>player</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 150011,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Since <code>Player</code> inherits from <code>Character</code>, it's a <strong>subclass</strong> of the <code>Character</code> class. The <code>Character</code> class, then, is its <strong>superclass</strong>.</p><p>Make sure the <code>Player</code> class inherits the properties of its superclass, <code>Character</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"70\" endIndex=\"76\" /><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"84\" /><option startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"94\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Character\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Character\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>Player</code>, followed by <code>extends</code>, and finally <code>Character</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 150012,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does it mean when we say class <code>A</code> inherited from class <code>B</code>?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Class <code>A</code> can access all of class <code>B</code>'s properties and methods</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">They can access each other's properties and methods</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Class <code>A</code> can access all of class <code>B</code>'s properties and methods.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 150013,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the keyword to make a class inherit from another?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>extends</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>inherits</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>extends</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 150014,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we call a class that other classes inherit from?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Superclass</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">General class</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick Superclass.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 150015,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does the subclass inherit from the superclass?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"2\" correct=\"true\">Its methods and properties</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Its name</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Its methods and properties.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 150016,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Make the <code>Boss</code> class inherit from the <code>Enemy</code> class.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"74\" endIndex=\"81\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Enemy\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(level) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".level = level;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Boss\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Enemy\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>extends</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 150017,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create an object from the <code>Boss</code> class and display it.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"105\" endIndex=\"108\" /><option startIndex=\"109\" endIndex=\"113\" /><option startIndex=\"114\" endIndex=\"115\" /><option startIndex=\"130\" endIndex=\"135\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Enemy\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(level) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".level = level;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Boss\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Enemy\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemy = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Boss(\" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemy);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>new</code> followed by <code>Boss</code> and then <code>5</code>, <code>enemy</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 150018,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Make sure the <code>Boss</code> class inherits the properties of its superclass, <code>Enemy</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"73\" /><option startIndex=\"74\" endIndex=\"81\" /><option startIndex=\"82\" endIndex=\"87\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Enemy\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(level) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".level = level;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Boss\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Enemy\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>Boss</code>, followed by <code>extends</code>, and finally <code>Enemy</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17688,
        "title": "Inheritance Advanced",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 150019,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If a subclass doesn't have a <code>constructor()</code> method, the superclass' constructor becomes the <strong>default constructor</strong>.</p><p>The <code>name</code> property of <code>player</code> gets created through the <code>Entity</code> class' constructor. Try and access it.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"entity.name\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"140\" endIndex=\"146\" /><option startIndex=\"146\" endIndex=\"147\" /><option startIndex=\"147\" endIndex=\"151\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Player(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Rogue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(player.name);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>player</code>, followed by <code>.</code>, and finally <code>name</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 150020,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A subclass also inherits its superclass' <strong>methods</strong>.</p><p>Try calling the <code>takeDamage()</code> method through the <code>Player</code> instance.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"250\" endIndex=\"256\" /><option startIndex=\"256\" endIndex=\"257\" /><option startIndex=\"257\" endIndex=\"267\" /><option startIndex=\"267\" endIndex=\"268\" /><option startIndex=\"268\" endIndex=\"270\" /><option startIndex=\"270\" endIndex=\"271\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" takeDamage(amount) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp -= amount;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; took &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + amount + \" /><text value=\"&quot; damage&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Player(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Knight&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"player.takeDamage(\" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>player</code> followed by <code>.</code> and then <code>takeDamage</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>10</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 150021,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can create as many subclasses of <code>Entity</code> as we want. They'll <em>all</em> have access to the properties of the <code>Entity</code> class.</p><p>Make the <code>Enemy</code> class inherit from the <code>Entity</code> class and call <code>takeDamage()</code> on an <code>Enemy</code> object.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"219\" endIndex=\"224\" /><option startIndex=\"225\" endIndex=\"232\" /><option startIndex=\"233\" endIndex=\"239\" /><option startIndex=\"342\" endIndex=\"352\" /><option startIndex=\"352\" endIndex=\"353\" /><option startIndex=\"353\" endIndex=\"355\" /><option startIndex=\"355\" endIndex=\"356\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" takeDamage(amount) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp -= amount;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; took &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + amount + \" /><text value=\"&quot; damage&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Enemy\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Player(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Knight&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemy = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Enemy(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"player.takeDamage(\" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"enemy.takeDamage(\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>Enemy</code> followed by <code>extends</code> and then <code>Entity</code>, <code>takeDamage</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>12</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 150022,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Inheritance becomes useful when subclasses have <strong>additional functionality</strong>, like their own methods.</p><p>Only players can <code>heal()</code>. Add a <code>heal()</code> method to the <code>Player</code> class and call it.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"109\" endIndex=\"121\" /><option startIndex=\"235\" endIndex=\"241\" /><option startIndex=\"241\" endIndex=\"242\" /><option startIndex=\"242\" endIndex=\"250\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" heal(amount) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp += amount;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; healed &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + amount);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Player(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Cleric&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"player.heal(\" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>heal(amount)</code> followed by <code>player</code> and then <code>.</code>, <code>heal(20)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 150023,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Inheritance works <strong>one way</strong> only. Not all instances of <code>Entity</code> are a kind of <code>Player</code>, so they <em>can't</em> access specific <code>Player</code> functionality.</p><p>What would happen if we try to make the enemy <code>.heal();</code>, would it work?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(name) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name = name;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Player\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Entity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" heal(amount) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".hp += amount;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; healed &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + amount);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Player(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Cleric&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"player.heal(\" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemy = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" Entity(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Goblin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"enemy.heal(\" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">No, an error will show up</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Yes, enemies can always heal like players</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">No, an error will show up.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 150024,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How can we create an instance from <code>Level</code> with a set <code>difficulty</code> property?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Stage\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(difficulty) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".difficulty = difficulty;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Level\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Stage\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">With <code>const level = new Level(\"Hard\");</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We can't, because <code>Level</code> has no constructor with that property</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">With <code>const level = new Level(\"Hard\");</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 150025,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How might we set an active item slot for the <code>playerInventory</code> object?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Inventory\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"constructor\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(owner) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".owner = owner;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".activeSlot = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" setActiveSlot(slot) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"this\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\".activeSlot = slot;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"PlayerInventory\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"extends\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Inventory\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"{}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerInventory = \" /><text value=\"new\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" PlayerInventory(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Ranger&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">With <code>playerInventory.setActiveSlot(2);</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">With <code>Inventory.setActiveSlot(2);</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">With <code>playerInventory.setActiveSlot(2);</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 150026,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How many subclasses can you create from a superclass?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">As many as you want</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">At most ten</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">As many as you want.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 150027,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Can subclasses only use the methods that their superclass has?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">No, subclasses can also have methods of their own</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Subclasses <em>can't</em> have methods of their own</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">No, subclasses can also have methods of their own.</p></body></html>"
          },
